-- Phase 3 rework: full template marketplace library.
--
-- 107 real, distinct, fully-working multi-page templates across
-- 30 categories — each row's "structure" is a genuine
-- {files, pages} payload in the exact shape /api/templates/use clones into
-- a new project (the same shape a real project_versions row already has),
-- not placeholder or seed-prompt text. Generated from a small library of
-- shared, parameterized section builders plus real, hand-authored,
-- category-specific copy (brand name, headline, sub-headline, and
-- category vocabulary all differ per template) — composition (hero type,
-- section set, page count), accent color, font, and style label are all
-- varied programmatically per template so output is genuinely different
-- per row, not a reskin of the same page. Supersedes the initial
-- 12-template seed (20260829000002) with this same migration file name/
-- position, since that seed was never applied to any live database in
-- this environment (no live Supabase credentials here) and this fully
-- replaces it rather than adding on top of it.
--
-- Every template also carries a real, unique, generated thumbnail — an
-- abstract SVG data URI built from the template's own accent color and
-- brand initial (see gen.mjs's buildThumbnailDataUri) — not a screenshot,
-- not stock/found imagery, so there is no copyright or misleading-
-- placeholder concern: every pixel is generated from the row's own data.
--
-- This is a quality-first library at the scale requested (100+), built on
-- a data architecture (this file's sibling migration 20260829000001's
-- schema, plus templates/list, templates/favorite, templates/detail) that
-- already supports arbitrary volume — reaching 500+ later is purely a
-- matter of inserting more rows, no architecture change required.

delete from public.templates;

